    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8c515403",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: blacks_are_musical; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two men in suits, one appearing to be Black and the other white, in a physical struggle where the white man is grabbing the Black man's collar. The text overlay reads 'blacks are musical' at the top and 'they always love a good beat' at the bottom. The visual of a physical altercation is juxtaposed with the text to imply that Black people are inherently aggressive or violent, using the metaphor of 'a good beat' to suggest a connection to rhythm or music that is equated with aggression. This is a harmful and hateful stereotype that reduces a racial group to a simplistic, negative caricature, implying that their cultural expression (music) is inherently linked to violence or physicality. The meme uses racialized imagery and language to perpetuate a harmful and offensive stereotype, fitting the definition of hateful content as it directly attacks a group based on race.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_eb6c24e8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
